        },
        {
          "text": "**The Zettelkasten Method:** A study of the specific historical system developed by Niklas Luhmann that serves as the foundation for modern networked note-taking.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 93,
          "source": "topic-set-pkb-note-building-🆔20251018203446.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Progressive Summarization:** An exploration of Tiago Forte's specific technique for information processing in layers, which provides a structured method for note elaboration.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 95,
          "source": "topic-set-pkb-note-building-🆔20251018203446.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Maps of Content (MOCs):** A deeper dive into the concept of using \"notes about other notes\" as a flexible, emergent alternative to rigid folder structures.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 96,
          "source": "topic-set-pkb-note-building-🆔20251018203446.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Dataview Query Language (DQL):** A practical investigation into the syntax and application of the Dataview plugin itself, showing how a well-designed metadata system is put into practice.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 97,
          "source": "topic-set-pkb-note-building-🆔20251018203446.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The PARA Method:** An analysis of this popular system (Projects, Areas, Resources, Archives) as a high-level framework for *action-oriented* organization, and how it can coexist with a bottom-up note-linking system.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 98,
          "source": "topic-set-pkb-note-building-🆔20251018203446.md"
        }
      ]
